#Day 17 Notes – Todo List in React (Part 1)

1.State for input:
const [task, setTask] = useState("");

2.State for todos list:
const [todos, setTodos] = useState([]);

3.Controlled Input:
<input
value={task}
onChange={(e) => setTask(e.target.value)}
placeholder="Enter a task"
/>

4.Add Task Function:
function addTask() {
if (task.trim() === "") return;
setTodos([...todos, task]);
setTask("");
}

5.Render the List:
  {todos.map((todo, index) => (
    {todo}
  ))}

Key Points:
-value + onChange = Controlled Input
-...todos = keep old items and add new one
-.map() = show list of items
-key={index} = required when using map
